{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Staircase","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.Staircase","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.Hoefsmit"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.betaEWWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.betaEWWord","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Staircase.lean#L152-L194","doc":"Concrete realisation of the canonical `β_EW Δ_I^minimal` word\non `n` strands.\n\nThe Python reference (verbatim from `staircase_ew_predictions.py`):\n\n```python\ndef beta_ew_word(n_strands: int) -> list[int]:\n    if n_strands < 4: return [0, 1, 0]\n    delta_I = [1, 3, 1]\n    word = []\n    for k in range(0, n_strands - 1, 2):\n        word.extend([k] * 4 + delta_I)\n    return word\n```\n\nFor `n ≥ 5` we emit the `[2j] * 4 ++ [1, 3, 1]` block for every\n`j ∈ {0, 1, …, n/2 − 1}` whose anchor index `2j` fits in\n`Fin (n − 1)`; the in-range check is discharged by `omega` per\nblock.  For `3 ≤ n < 5` we emit the Python fallback\n`[σ₀, σ₁, σ₀]`.  For `n < 3` no generators exist and the word\nis empty.\n\n**Intentional deviation from the verbatim Python at `n = 4`.** The\nPython reference applies the `< 4` fallback (so `n = 4` enters the\nloop body), but the loop's `delta_I = [1, 3, 1]` writes index `3`,\nwhich is out of bounds in `Fin (n − 1) = Fin 3` for `n = 4` and\nwould not type-check on the Lean side. We therefore extend the\nfallback to `3 ≤ n < 5` so the construction stays well-typed. The\n`n = 4` case is not part of the staircase conjecture's testable\nregime (`staircaseStrands k = k(k+1)/2 ∈ {3, 6, 10, 15, …}`), so\nthis deviation does not weaken any downstream theorem.\n\nReplaces the previous `opaque` declaration so downstream\n`wordImage` calls see a concrete list rather than an unevaluable\nblack box. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.betaEWBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.betaEWBlock","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Staircase.lean#L122-L134","doc":"Concrete reproduction of one `β_EW` block: `[σ_k, σ_k, σ_k, σ_k, σ_1, σ_3, σ_1]`.\n\nRequires `5 ≤ n` so that index `3` fits in `Fin (n - 1)` (the `Δ_I`\nsub-word uses generator indices `1, 3`); the caller also passes a\nproof that the block's anchor index `2j` is in range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.deltaIMinimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.deltaIMinimal","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Staircase.lean#L114-L120","doc":"The canonical \"Δ_I^minimal\" sub-word `[1, 3, 1]` shared by all\n`β_EW` words on `n ≥ 4` strands.\n\nMatches `staircase_ew_predictions.beta_ew_word`'s `delta_I` constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.staircaseStrands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.staircaseStrands","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Staircase.lean#L110-L112","doc":"Number of strands for the canonical β_EW operator on `ρ k`:\n`n_k = k(k+1)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.staircasePartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.staircasePartition","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Staircase.lean#L96-L101","doc":"The staircase partition `ρ k = (k, k-1, …, 1) ⊢ k(k+1)/2`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:staircase-partition","label":"def:staircase-partition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/staircase-partition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.staircaseList_sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.staircaseList_sorted","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Staircase.lean#L84-L94","doc":"The staircase list is non-increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.staircaseList_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.staircaseList_le","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Staircase.lean#L73-L82","doc":"Membership in `staircaseList k`: every part is at most `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.staircaseList_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.staircaseList_positive","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Staircase.lean#L62-L71","doc":"Every part of the staircase is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.staircaseList_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.staircaseList_sum","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Staircase.lean#L46-L60","doc":"Sum of the staircase: `1 + 2 + … + k = k(k+1)/2`.\n\nUsed to discharge `Partition.sum_eq` for `staircasePartition`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.staircaseList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.staircaseList","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/Staircase.lean#L39-L44","doc":"The staircase shape `ρ k := (k, k-1, …, 1)` as a plain list.\nDefined recursively for clarity.  `staircaseList 0 = []`,\n`staircaseList 3 = [3, 2, 1]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}